{
  "scriptName": "Kana",
  "buttonLabel": "Kana Guide",
  "fontScale": 1.3,
  "intro": "Hiragana and katakana — the two Japanese syllable alphabets — with the pronunciation of every sound.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "How kana work",
      "text": [
        "Japanese is written with three scripts at once: hiragana for native words and grammar endings, katakana mainly for words borrowed from other languages (コーヒー, パソコン), and kanji — Chinese characters — for most nouns, verbs and adjectives.",
        "Each kana stands for one syllable-like beat (a mora). Hiragana and katakana are two sets of shapes for the same sounds, so learning one chart teaches you the sounds of both.",
        "The romaji under each sound is the usual spelling in Latin letters; the IPA in brackets shows how it is actually pronounced in standard Tokyo Japanese."
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Symbols used in the pronunciations",
      "text": "The pronunciations in this app use the International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA). Most letters sound as in English; these are the ones that don't, with an example word from the vocabulary.",
      "items": [
        {
          "char": "ꜜ",
          "ipa": "箸 [haꜜɕi]",
          "note": "pitch drops after this point; no ꜜ = flat"
        },
        {
          "char": "ː",
          "ipa": "お母さん [okaꜜːsaɴ]",
          "note": "long — hold the vowel for two beats"
        },
        {
          "char": "◌̥",
          "ipa": "学生 [ɡakɯ̥seː]",
          "note": "whispered, nearly silent vowel"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɴ",
          "ipa": "本 [hoꜜɴ]",
          "note": "ん at the end of a word — n made at the back of the mouth"
        },
        {
          "char": "ŋ",
          "ipa": "銀行 [ɡiŋkoː]",
          "note": "ng as in sing"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɲ",
          "ipa": "兄 [aꜜɲi]",
          "note": "n with the tongue flat, like ny"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɯ",
          "ipa": "夜 [joꜜɾɯ]",
          "note": "u with relaxed, unrounded lips"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɾ",
          "ipa": "夜 [joꜜɾɯ]",
          "note": "quick tap — between r, l and d"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɕ",
          "ipa": "私 [ɰataɕi]",
          "note": "soft sh, tongue flat"
        },
        {
          "char": "tɕ",
          "ipa": "友達 [tomodatɕi]",
          "note": "soft ch"
        },
        {
          "char": "dʑ",
          "ipa": "時間 [dʑikaɴ]",
          "note": "soft j"
        },
        {
          "char": "ç",
          "ipa": "人 [çi̥toꜜ]",
          "note": "h before i — like a whispered y (German ich)"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɸ",
          "ipa": "お風呂 [oɸɯꜜɾo]",
          "note": "f blown through both lips, no teeth"
        },
        {
          "char": "ɰ",
          "ipa": "電話 [deɴɰa]",
          "note": "w without rounding the lips"
        },
        {
          "char": "ʲ",
